---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
	title="Terms of Service | STLACCESS"
	description="Terms and conditions for using the STLACCESS conversion engine. Fair use, liability disclaimers, and project independence."
>
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-20 w-full">
        <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
        <nav class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 pt-12 pb-4 text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-600">
            <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#ff6b35]">Home</a> 
            <span class="mx-2 text-slate-800">/</span> 
            <span class="text-slate-400">Terms of Service</span>
        </nav>

        <!-- Header -->
        <div class="mb-16">
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold font-heading mb-6 tracking-tight">Terms of <span class="text-[#ff6b35]">Service</span></h1>
            <p class="text-lg text-slate-400 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">Plain English rules for using STLACCESS. I keep it simple so you can get back to printing.</p>
        </div>

        <section class="space-y-16">
            
            <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none space-y-12 text-slate-300">
                
                <div class="space-y-6">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
                    <p>
                        By accessing STLACCESS.com, you agree to these terms. If you don't agree, please do not use the tool. I reserve the right to update these terms as the project evolves.
                    </p>
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-6">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading">2. Use of the Service</h2>
                    <p>
                        STLACCESS is a free tool provided for the 3D printing and tabletop gaming community.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-4">
                        <li><strong>Fair Use:</strong> You are free to use my conversion values for your personal and commercial 3D printing projects.</li>
                        <li><strong>Restrictions:</strong> You may not use automated scripts to scrape our data or attempt to disrupt the service through malicious traffic.</li>
                        <li><strong>Embeds:</strong> The Creator Badge is provided for use by sculptors and storefronts. Modification of the badge's code to misrepresent scale verification is prohibited.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-6 bg-red-500/5 border border-red-500/20 p-8 rounded-[2.5rem]">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading">3. Liability Disclaimer (The "Print" Clause)</h2>
                    <p>
                        3D printing is a complex process involving many variables.
                    </p>
                    <p class="font-bold text-white">
                        STLACCESS provides mathematical conversions based on standard baselines. I am NOT liable for:
                    </p>
                    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-4">
                        <li>Wasted resin or filament due to print failures.</li>
                        <li>Discrepancies caused by resin shrinkage or slicer settings.</li>
                        <li>Incorrect scale results if the source file was not sculpted to the stated baseline.</li>
                        <li>Physical damage to hardware or injury resulting from the use of 3D printing equipment.</li>
                    </ul>
                    <p class="text-sm italic">In short: I provide the math, but the print is your responsibility. Always run a small test piece if precision is critical.</p>
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-6">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading">4. Intellectual Property & Affiliation</h2>
                    <p>
                        STLACCESS is an <strong>independent project</strong>.
                    </p>
                    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-4">
                        <li>I am not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by Games Workshop, Atomic Mass Games, Wizards of the Coast, or any other miniature manufacturer.</li>
                        <li>Product names and game systems (e.g., "Warhammer 40,000", "Star Wars Legion") are trademarks of their respective owners and are used here for reference and identification purposes only.</li>
                    </ul>
                </div>

                <div class="space-y-6">
                    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading">5. Governing Law</h2>
                    <p>
                        As a global tool, I strive for worldwide compliance. However, these terms are governed by the laws of the jurisdiction in which the project operates. For data protection details, see my <a href="/privacy" class="text-white border-b border-white/20 hover:text-[#ff6b35] transition-colors">Privacy Policy</a>.
                    </p>
                </div>

            </div>
        </section>
    </div>
</Layout>
